   "blocking": true,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "Encapsulating CTransaction and removing const member variables risks mutability footguns and introduces broad churn across consensus-critical code for no immediate benefit.",
   "hash": "2655d32295115d4e",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:58+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "c:4758920204",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:4758920204",
   "kind": "approach",
   "other_replies": [],
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "This doesn't seem like a good idea at all to me. If you want an object that can represent different transactions over its lifetime, you should be using CMutableTransaction",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35569#issuecomment-4758920204"
  },
  {
   "after_reply": "likely_settled",
   "after_reply_note": "resolved by deleting copy-assignment operator",
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-06-22",
   "author": "josibake",
   "author_replies": [
    "c:4768281519"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "402500baad826efff3dbe52c75694d93121e1b06"
   },
   "harm": "As long as CTransactionRef shares the CTransaction wrapper, allowing assignment leaves a potential non-const alias footgun.",
   "hash": "3b4365a2bdb12019",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:58+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "c:4767696750",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:4767696750",
   "kind": "safety",
   "other_replies": [],
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "As long as CTransactionRef shares the CTransaction wrapper, making that wrapper assignable leaves a possible non-const-alias footgun.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-06-23",
    "by": "josibake",
    "id": "c:4779007846",
    "quote": "Thanks for taking the suggestions regarding removing the assignment operator, and removing the default move constructor."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35569#issuecomment-4767696750"
  },
  {
   "after_reply": "likely_settled",
   "after_reply_note": "resolved by deleting default move constructor",
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-06-22",
   "author": "josibake",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:3453258513"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "402500baad826efff3dbe52c75694d93121e1b06"
   },
   "harm": "Default move constructor on non-const members could memberwise move vin/vout vectors and leave invalid cached witness/hash fields on the moved-from instance.",
   "hash": "98a104070a0dcb92",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:58+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3453169670",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3453169670",
   "kind": "safety",
   "other_replies": [],
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "vin/vout, being vectors, move could actually mean move the underlying storage. In light of that, I think we should delete the move constructer during the transition.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-06-23",
    "by": "josibake",
    "id": "c:4779007846",
    "quote": "Thanks for taking the suggestions regarding removing the assignment operator, and removing the default move constructor."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35569#discussion_r3453169670"
  },
  {
   "after_reply": "likely_settled",
   "after_reply_note": "resolved by adding LIFETIMEBOUND",
